course: dictionary
lesson: 3285
title: Esperanto, a language made for everyone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Esperanto is a language that was invented, not one that grew up slowly in a single country. L. L. Zamenhof, a doctor from Poland, made it more than a hundred years ago so that people from different countries could talk easily in one simple shared language.
explain: «Esperanto was invented in 1887 by L. L. Zamenhof.» The word invented is a clue: someone thought it up on purpose, and it did not happen by itself over many years like English did.
explain: Esperanto's grammar is very regular, which means it follows the same rules each time. «In Esperanto, mal- makes the opposite (granda big, malgranda small), and -j makes plurals, on describing words too: bela kato, belaj katoj.» Once you know the rules, you can work out new words.
fact: Esperanto is a made-up language, also called a constructed language.
fact: «Esperanto» was invented more than a hundred years ago by L. L. Zamenhof, a doctor from Poland.
fact: In Esperanto, nouns end in -o and describing words end in -a.
fact: The prefix «mal-» makes a word mean its opposite: «varma» is warm, and «malvarma» is cold.
fact: The name Esperanto means «one who hopes», so in stories it can show a character who loves languages or dreams of peace.
exercise: «Esperanto was invented in 1887 by L. L. Zamenhof.» Who invented Esperanto? | A king from France | A sailor from Brazil | *A doctor from Poland | A teacher from Japan
exercise: In Esperanto, «mal-» makes the opposite. What is the opposite of «granda», big? | *malgranda | granda | bela | varma
exercise: «Bela kato» becomes «belaj katoj». What does the -j do? | Makes a word the opposite | *Makes words plural, on describing words too | Makes a word a question | Makes a word the past tense
test: What does the name Esperanto mean? | Shared food | A small country | *One who hopes | Speak clearly
test: Why did L. L. Zamenhof invent Esperanto? | To write poems about the sea | To teach dogs to talk | *So that people from different countries could talk easily in one shared language | To make a secret code for spies
exam: Which word describes how Esperanto came to be? | *Invented | Ancient | Lost | Natural
